At this point, you might be wondering how we create such beautiful, detailed renders? Let us introduce you to the world of FUSED RENDERING KERNELS and how real-time rendering engines desperately need them in order to survive in a world where video games and effects must render in real-time, with photorealistic quality, and at 4K resolution.

The old way to create a depth map was to simply perform the depth calculation, store the results in memory, and query the results later—pretty straightforward, right? Creating useful information for rendering is laborious, however, especially if you want to use all of the features that are currently available in Autodesk Maya and 3ds Max. This is extremely apparent in scenes with millions of triangles and bits and pieces with complicated features such as fur or hair. Render calculations become even more bizarre with complex, glass materials.

