Figure 1 shows the average distribution among parts of speech for each temperature category. At a glance, we notice the general consistency of language model output between each temperature category. Surprisingly, we notice the generally higher frequency of verbs and adverbs for higher temperatures. While verbs are statistically insignificant, the difference in adverbs is significant (\(p < 10^{-14}\)), and might suggest that higher temperature generally leads to more descriptive language.

