🧠 LLM Response:
 Stop sequences are a method for defining specific conditions under which our generation should end. A stop sequence is simply a string that the model may use to stop generating more tokens. When the generation reaches a sequence that matches the stop sequence, generation ends immediately.

Here is an example using the Playground and a stop sequence of `</s>`. You must make sure that you include the stop sequence in your generation prompt.

**Note: The `</s>` token is a special stop token that AI21 Studio uses to automatically determine the end of a sentence. You do not need to use this token as a stop sequence.**

<iframe height="430" style="width: 100%;" scrolling="no" title="Stop Sequences Example" src="//codepen.io/AI21Labs/embed/ExeJPqd/?height=430&theme-id=dark&default-tab=result" frameborder="no" loading="lazy" allowtransparency="true" allowfullscreen="true">
