</iframe>

In addition to using a stop sequence to determine when generation ends, we can also use sample inputs for predicting the next few generation steps. We call this behavior "**refix**".

A refix sample input is a text string of about 1000 characters or less. In case the input string it is too long, the API will consider only the first 1000 characters.

When we provide a refix sample input, we get permission to use this sample input or a part of it for creating up to the 10 first outputs, based on the contextual input.

For further details about refix, see [here](https://docs.ai21.com/-/ai21-studio-simpletokens#/ai21%2Fstudio%2Fsimpletokens-v1-generateText?id=_refix).

Prefix and refix text will be prioritized over the stop sequence and will be displayed in the output.

**Note: Stop sequences currently only work with the API endpoints in AI21 Studio. The Web App does not currently support stop sequences.**

