[103/200] Running: What is Triton Inference Server?...

🧠 LLM Response:


Triton Inference Server enables machine learning models to be deployed from any framework and with high performance and high scalability, using an open-source, GPU accelerated, multi-node, and multi-framework server.

What are the Triton Server options?

- Triton Server can be deployed in a Docker container for easy deployment in the cloud or on-premise. The Docker container is available on Docker Hub and it is designed to leverage NVIDIA GPU’s for acceleration.
- Triton Server can also be deployed on the NVIDIA EGX platform. EGX is a platform for building and deploying AI applications at the edge. Triton Server on EGX can query models running on many edge devices and aggregate the results back to the cloud.
- Triton Server is available as an Amazon Machine Image (AMI) and it is deployed in a GPU optimized virtual machine on AWS.
- Triton Server is also available for Arm based servers and can be deployed on Amazon Arm available with Graviton processors.

The OpenVINO toolkit and its model optimizer and inference engine are supported in Triton Server. What are the prerequisites to use OpenVINO models in Triton Server?

- Triton Server only supports IR format models produced by OpenVINO model optimizer. The IR format models are OpenVINO Intermediate Representation files, ‘.xml’ and ‘.bin’.
- Hierarchy of key-value encoding specified in the OpenVINO toolkit model optimizer is supported natively in Triton Server.
- The datatypes used in the models (float, int8, or int16) are converted to constant enums used in Triton Server to support the OpenVINO to Triton Server workflow. C++ implementation of OpenVINO models will have to convert the OpenVINO data types to Triton Server constant enums.
- FP16 (half-precision) floats are supported for OpenVINO models.
- When using the OpenVINO Inference Engine executable plugin, it is a requirement to set the Triton Server ENABLE_GPU environment variable as 1.

If I have ResNet-50 OpenVINO model, can I use the model directly in Triton Server?

Yes. If you have a Resnet50 OpenVINO model,

    .

