How does GPU acceleration work in Triton Server?

Triton Server supports multiple plugins. One among them is the OpenVINO GPU plugin, which is the default. This plugin allows you to GPU accelerate your OpenVINO model IR files. The OpenVINO plugin allows you to perform dynamic batching of models, real-time shape inference and tensor memory up to an entire CUDA device.

How does OpenVINO GPU and OpenVINO CPU plugin differ in Triton Server?

The OpenVINO GPU plugin allows you to run inference for a single model in GPU. The OpenVINO CPU plugin allows you to run inference for multiple models simultaneously as the number of models will get distributed in the GPU.

Can I use OpenVINO INT8 with Triton Server?

Yes. Triton Server supports OpenVINO INT8 quantization with the OpenVINO plugin.
