[141/200] Running: What are model shards and when are they used?...

🧠 LLM Response:


Model shards are components or pieces from your entire trained ML model.

They are used in multiple scenarios, for instance,

1. When you train a model on highly concurrent (more flows) and high data throughput (more volume of data), if you want to cut down on your training time, you can use parallelization to train different shards of the model together on different devices or servers on the same time.
2. You can use model shards to reduce both your training and inference time significantly by using multiple gpus and cpus to train and deliver the model.

Model sharding helps the model to learn more correlation between multiple pieces of data that individual model may not generalize.

Such as a model trained on a single shard can not detect the meaning of Sentiments properly, but when multiple shards are used to train together the model can generalize the meaning of Sentiments.

