[151/200] Running: What is a prompt-truncation error?...

🧠 LLM Response:


A prompt-truncation error happens when the words in a line of a prompt do not fit the size of the command line (e.g. terminal).

How to solve it?

You can avoid a prompt-truncation error by using a smaller prompt or by increasing the size of the command line.

For instance, I like to use the following prompt in my Terminal, which is quite large. Therefore, I increase the size of my terminal window (without any sidebar showing) to 170x47:

```
#!/bin/bash
export PS1='✔[\u@\h \W]\\$\[\033[01;32m\]> \[\033[1;37m\]'
export PROMPT_COMMAND=history -a  # Save and synchronize command history after every command.
export SUDO_PROMPT='☛[\u@\h \W] (sudo) %p% '
export HISTCONTROL=ignoredups  # Avoid running the same command twice.
```

What explains this so-called "80-column limit" in programming?

The "80-column limit" was set because this was the length of computer screens in the past. Nowadays, this limit still is being used by people in order to maintain a more readable and understandable text, when you open and edit a text-file that is 25/30 years old. Because, back then, computer screens could only display 80 columns.

Furthermore, to read most newspapers, you can hold it at arm's length. Reading a newspaper is, in that sense, kind of similar to reading at a computer-screen: if you are able to read a newspaper at arm's length, then your computer screen is at the ideal distance for reading. The width of a newspaper is about 80 characters.

Reading from different screens (left eyes @ laptops, right eyes @ notebooks, both eyes @ tablets, pressure sensitive display @ touchscreens, etc.) also benefit from a less wordy and more visually appealing textarea and thus well establish 80 characters x 25 lines (maximized for write-readibility). So by ‘squeezing’ in paragraphs, paragraph layouts, code snippets, rows, columns, array-data and other large data in only 80 columns, any text in a "technical" document is optimized for reading and writing.

Sources:

https://stackoverflow.com/questions/38482007/why-do-programming-courses-teach-the-80-character-limit-when-their-outputs-are/38482408#38482408

https://writing.stackexchange.com/questions/13000/why-does-the-80-character-limit-despite-wider-screens-still-stay-and-for-quo

https://stackoverflow.com/questions/175498/ideal-column-length-for-text/175636#175636

http://invisible-island.net/ncurses/ncurses.faq.html#LINE_LENGTH

