Comment: @Bernhard exactly that's why I wrote it because of the syntax error.

## Answer (1)

Finally I figured it out.

As @Fravadona suggested, the API sends the JSON tokens well but the problem is on my end where I was pipelining the output which in turn messes the JSON tokens.

To fix that, the only thing I needed to do was to read the output into the variable and then breaking the tokens into the array.

Here is the sample pipeline :

```
output=$(curl -S -s "http://example.com/v1/chunks/project/export?auth=TOKEN")

for entry in $(echo "${output}" | fgrep '"content":' | sed -e 's/"content"://g' -e 's/[{}]//g' -e 's/,/\n/g')
do
    stream_data+=("$entry")
done
```
